## Original Content
The film, from 'No Other Land' directors Yuval Abraham and Rachel Szor and produced by the Oscar-winning team behind 'The Zone of Interest,' was shot from the rooftops of Tel Aviv and documents Israel's bombing of Gaza.

## Summary
The New York Film Festival has added the North American premiere of 'NAZA', a documentary directed by Yuval Abraham and Rachel Szor, which captures Israel's bombing of Gaza from the rooftops of Tel Aviv. Produced by the Oscar-winning team behind 'The Zone of Interest', the film offers a unique perspective on the conflict. The premiere highlights the festival's commitment to showcasing impactful documentaries.

## Key Points
- 'NAZA' documentary to have North American premiere at New York Film Festival
- Directed by Yuval Abraham and Rachel Szor, known for 'No Other Land'
- Documents Israel's bombing of Gaza from Tel Aviv rooftops
- Produced by Oscar-winning team behind 'The Zone of Interest'


